    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green. The change is complete. Here's a summary of what I implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded an `ageBand` field to the owner API, derived from an optional `birthDate` request field, computed against the owner's `registrationDate`.\n\n**Spec/DTOs** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)\n- Added `birthDate` (ISO date, optional) to the `OwnerFields` request schema.\n- Added `ageBand` (read-only string) to the `Owner` response schema. The DTOs are generated from this spec at build time.\n\n**Domain model** (`model/Owner.java`)\n- Added a persisted `birthDate` (`LocalDate`, `birth_date DATE` column) with getter/setter, so the value round-trips through create \u2192 store \u2192 read.\n\n**Derivation** (`rest/function/owner/AgeBand.java`)\n- New helper `AgeBand.of(birthDate, registrationDate)` returning `MINOR` (< 18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+), or `null` when either date is absent. It uses completed years (`Period.between`) against the stored registration date \u2014 the effective, business-day-rolled date \u2014 matching the existing derived-field pattern (`Locality`, `ContactPreference`, etc.).\n\n**Mapping** (`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`)\n- Added the `ageBand` mapping expression. `birthDate` maps automatically by name (request\u2192entity and entity\u2192response).\n\n**Schema/data**\n- Added `birth_date DATE` to all four DB schemas (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres), and added the corresponding `NULL` to the positional seed inserts in `hsqldb/data.sql` (the DB the tests use).\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreDerivesAgeBand` (birthDate `1990-01-01` \u2192 `ADULT`) and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
